  <name>Xfig</name>
  <summary>Vector graphics drawing application</summary>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">org.xfig.xfig.desktop</launchable>
  <developer id="org.xfig">
    <name>Thomas Loimer</name>
  </developer>
  <update_contact>thomas.loimer_at_tuwien.ac.at</update_contact>
  <description>
    <p>
      Xfig is an X Window System tool for creating basic vector graphics,
      including bezier curves, lines, rulers and more.  The resulting
      graphics can be saved, printed on PostScript printers or converted to
      a variety of other formats (e.g., X11 bitmaps, Encapsulated
      PostScript, LaTeX).
    </p>
    <p>
      You should install xfig if you need a simple program to create vector
      graphics.
    </p>
  </description>
